 283:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****  ===============================================================================
 284:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     [..] This section provides the following functions:
 285:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_MultiProcessorEx_AddressLength_Set() API optionally sets the UART node address
 286:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****          detection length to more than 4 bits for multiprocessor address mark wake up.
 287:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** #if defined(USART_CR1_UESM)
 288:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_StopModeWakeUpSourceConfig() API defines the wake-up from stop mode
 289:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****          trigger: address match, Start Bit detection or RXNE bit status.
 290:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_EnableStopMode() API enables the UART to wake up the MCU from stop mode
 291:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****      (+) HAL_UARTEx_DisableStopMode() API disables the above functionality
 292:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** #endif
 293:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 294:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     [..] This subsection also provides a set of additional functions providing enhanced reception
 295:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     services to user. (For example, these functions allow application to handle use cases
 296:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     where number of data to be received is unknown).
 297:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 298:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) Compared to standard reception services which only consider number of received
 299:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         data elements as reception completion criteria, these functions also consider additional ev
 300:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****         as triggers for updating reception status to caller :
 301:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Detection of inactivity period (RX line has not been active for a given period).
 302:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****           (++) RX inactivity detected by IDLE event, i.e. RX line has been in idle state (normally 
 303:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****                for 1 frame time, after last received byte.
 304:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****           (++) RX inactivity detected by RTO, i.e. line has been in idle state
 305:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****                for a programmable time, after last received byte.
 306:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Detection that a specific character has been received.
 307:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c **** 
 308:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****     (#) There are two mode of transfer:
 309:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Blocking mode: The reception is performed in polling mode, until either expected number 
 310:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            or till IDLE event occurs. Reception is handled only during function execution.
 311:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            When function exits, no data reception could occur. HAL status and number of actually re
 312:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            are returned by function after finishing transfer.
 313:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****        (+) Non-Blocking mode: The reception is performed using Interrupts or DMA.
 314:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            These API's return the HAL status.
 315:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
 316:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            dedicated UART IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when using DMA mode.
 317:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****            The HAL_UARTEx_RxEventCallback() user callback will be executed during Receive process
ARM GAS  C:\Users\ADMINI~1\AppData\Local\Temp\cchQt67W.s 			page 7


